 <subsection xml:id="password-checker">
  <title>Password Checker</title>
<p>
    A strong password typically meets the following criteria:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Is at least 12 characters</li>
    <li>Contains uppercase and lowercase letters</li>
    <li>Contains numbers</li>
    <li>
      Contains special characters: <c>~`!@#$%^&amp;*() _-+={[}]|\\:;\"\'&gt;,&lt;.?/</c>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Create a Python program that determines whether a user's password is strong or weak. 
    The program should prompt the user to enter their password, then determine whether 
    it meets all requirements. It will then print whether the password is <q>Strong</q> or <q>Weak.</q>
  </p>

    <p>Program Requirements</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>Define a function <c>check_password</c> with a single parameter that is the user's password:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <p>Check the length of the password. If it is shorter than 12 characters:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Print <q>Your password is not long enough.</q></li>              
              <li>Do not complete the other checks if the password is too short</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>Create boolean variables for upper, lower, number, and special</li>
          <li>
            <p>Loop through each letter in the password:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>If it is uppercase, set upper to true</li>
              <li>If it is lowercase, set lower to true</li>
              <li>If it is a number, set number to true</li>
              <li>If it is a special character, set special to true</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li><p>Print the results of the requirements that are not met:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><q>Your password does not contain any numbers.</q></li>
              <li><q>Your password does not contain any uppercase letters.</q></li>
              <li><q>Your password does not contain any lowercase letters.</q></li>
              <li><q>Your password does not contain any special characters.</q></li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>If all four boolean values are true, print <q>Your password is strong</q></li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>After (and outside) the function:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Prompt the user to enter a password</li>
          <li>Call the <c>check_password</c> function with the user's password as an argument</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <table xml:id="table-password-check">
  <title>Password Validation Requirements and Outputs</title>
  <tabular halign="left">
    <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
      <cell>Input</cell>
      <cell>Output</cell>
    </row>
    <row bottom="minor">
      <cell>Password12!</cell>
      <cell>Your password is not long enough.</cell>
    </row>
    <row bottom="minor">
      <cell>abcdefghijkl</cell>
      <cell>
        <p>Your password does not contain any numbers.</p>
        <p>Your password does not contain any uppercase letters.</p>
        <p>Your password does not contain any special characters.</p>
      </cell>
    </row>
    <row bottom="minor">
      <cell>ABCDEFJGHIJLKL123!</cell>
      <cell>
        Your password does not contain any lowercase letters.
      </cell>
    </row>
    <row bottom="minor">
      <cell>SecurePassword!</cell>
      <cell>Your password does not contain any numbers.</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>SecurePass123!</cell>
      <cell>Your password is strong.</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>
</table>

<p>
  Use the following string methods to check each character in your password:
</p>

<ul>
  <li><c>letter.isupper()</c> - returns True if the letter is uppercase</li>
  <li><c>letter.islower()</c> - returns True if the letter is lowercase</li>
  <li><c>letter.isdigit()</c> - returns True if the letter is a number</li>
  <li><c>letter.isalnum()</c> - returns True if the letter is a letter or number, False if it is a special character</li>
</ul>

